          "rationale": "Section 4.1 (p0024) is the only renewal provision in the Agreement. Each renewal term is one year, which is acceptable, but the sole exit is 90 days' written notice, i.e. a 90-day non-renewal notice window that fails the 60-day fallback ceiling on a material term (though not itself walk-away, which requires windows longer than 90 days or multi-year renewals). The Agreement grants no renewal price-uplift right, since Section 3.1 fixes consideration as a 30% share of Net Sales, so the price-cap element is not triggered. We therefore target the fallback: the 90-day period is removed from the renewal sentence and the exit is stated in operative text as sixty (60) days' prior written notice, retaining the mutual either-Party right, the one-year renewal term, the anniversary mechanic and the \"Termination Date\" definition. The preferred 30-day opt-out with a 60-day HDI reminder is a rationale note only.",
